virglrenderer: the blitter's shaders use a GLSL version core profiles accept

What: the GL blitter's desktop shaders were "#version 130". The version line now
follows the host's GLSL version, the same number the shader translator gets
(vrend_renderer_get_glsl_version(), new): 4.00 if the host has it (macOS: 4.10),
1.50 from 1.50, else 1.30 as before. The ARB_texture_multisample (colour and
depth multisample blits) and ARB_texture_cube_map_array "#extension" lines are
left out where that version has them in core, and depth blits from cube map
arrays get the cube map array line below 4.00 (they did not compile there,
an upstream bug). GLES is unchanged.
Why: Apple's core profile refuses GLSL 1.30, so the blit vertex shader failed at
every QEMU start ("version '130' is not supported") and every blit that needs a
shader (format conversion, swizzle, sRGB, depth, multisample resolve to another
format) drew nothing.
Upstreamable; not sent.
Tests: Tests/virgl/test-blitter-shaders.c (builds the blitter's real shaders for
every target and type with the Mac's OpenGL and links them; depth blits also
at GLSL 1.50).
